From: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 09:19:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 069/214] spmi: mtk-pmif: Fix the SID decode of RCS interrupts

Each SPMI_SLV_x_EINT register holds the RCS flags of four SIDs, eight
bits each, but the chained handler finds the SID of a flag with bit / 7.
A flag in bit 7 of a SID's byte is then credited to the next SID, and
the handler clears that SID's byte instead of the flag, so it never
leaves its loop.

Divide by the eight bits per SID.
---
 drivers/spmi/spmi-mtk-pmif.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/spmi/spmi-mtk-pmif.c b/drivers/spmi/spmi-mtk-pmif.c
index c472fd4bd..b1c147c3e 100644
--- a/drivers/spmi/spmi-mtk-pmif.c
+++ b/drivers/spmi/spmi-mtk-pmif.c
@@ -513,7 +513,8 @@ static void mtk_spmi_handle_chained_irq(struct irq_desc *desc)
 
 		while (val) {
 			u8 bit = __ffs(val);
-			u8 bank = bit / 7;
+			u8 bank = bit / 8;
+
 			u8 sid = ((i - SPMI_SLV_3_0_EINT) * 4) + bank;
 
 			val &= ~(PMIF_RCS_IRQ_MASK << (8 * bank));
